# EBWiki Code Quality & Engineering Rules

Follow these rules when editing EBWiki. Full details: docs/CODE_QUALITY_RULES.md

## Pre-commit & CI
- Run rubocop, brakeman, rspec before committing. Use `bundle exec pre-commit install`.
- Do not push failing checks. CI must pass for PRs.

## Code Style
- Pass rubocop. No new offenses. Max 100 chars/line, 35 lines/block.
- Avoid `rubocop:disable` without a tracked issue.

## Testing
- Add specs for new features, services, and non-trivial changes.
- Use FactoryBot. Specs must be independent.

## Architecture
- Use service objects (`include Service`, `call(...)`) for business logic.
- Keep controllers thin; delegate to services/models.
- Single responsibility; explicit over implicit.

## Security
- No new Brakeman warnings. Use strong params. No secrets in code.

## Error Handling
- Rescue specific exceptions; log errors. No silent failures.

## Git & PRs
- Branch per feature. One logical change per PR.
- Clear commit messages; reference issues when relevant.

## General
- DRY, YAGNI, readability. Update docs when behavior changes.
